  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bamboo from Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There seems to be an opportunity to transfer bamboo and waste from wood sawing companies in Ghana into bamboo/wood briquets, that can be used as an energy provider. With this project, Bambooruko B.V. is testing the production of bamboo briquets and its production process. The farmed bamboo is locally processed, to do so sustainably trainings have been provided on clump management. A total of 12 people have been trained and the DGGF-TA financing has led to the creation of a local entity which will employ 5 people and lead to 15 indirect FTE linked to the farmers. The research has shown that there is enough bamboo in the region to produce with and to complement this, new varieties will be introduced.</narrative>
  </description>
